    {
      "src": "> [!summary]\n> The reference transform is proved TP1 for every text and to preserve content, and every small case is checked exhaustively; lesson 1's tiling closes any grid of squares that TP1 closes. The protocol, the store's conditional write, the document format and what a position counts are outside the proofs, and are tested or argued. A port is tested against the reference's vectors and against the reference itself on random inputs. Running the reference compiled to WebAssembly is possible, on a Tier 2 platform, with a runtime built for wasm32 and small stacks, and the compilers are trusted, not proved.",
